%% Required pod anti-affinity — Deployment Targets & Scheduling, lab exercise 2 ("You'll end with").
%% requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution on kubernetes.io/hostname: each claims replica needs a
%% node that holds no other replica, so one replica more than there are eligible nodes stays Pending
%% with a FailedScheduling event instead of doubling up on a node.
%% Shape (diagram-size-guard): LR, longest chain 4 nodes, no subgraph, labels at most 2 lines.
flowchart LR
  RULE["required anti-affinity<br/>per hostname"] --> ONE["one claims pod<br/>per node"]
  ONE --> FULL["every eligible node<br/>holds one"]
  FULL -.->|"one more replica"| PEND["Pending<br/>FailedScheduling"]
  classDef hi fill:#e00,stroke:#900,color:#fff;
  classDef done fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#137333,color:#0d652d;
  classDef gone fill:#fce8e6,stroke:#c5221f,color:#a50e0e;
  class RULE hi;
  class ONE,FULL done;
  class PEND gone;
